course: dictionary
lesson: 14382
title: Which way is it facing?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Orientation is about direction: which way something faces or points. «The map was held in the wrong orientation, so we walked the wrong way.» The clue is walked the wrong way: the map was turned the wrong direction.
explain: At school, orientation can mean a short welcome. «On orientation day, the new pupils toured the school and found the library.» Here orientation means a visit that helps new pupils learn their way around.
explain: In maths, a shape can be turned, and its orientation changes while its size and shape stay the same. «The page was turned to landscape orientation, so it was wide, not tall.» A page can be in portrait orientation (tall) or landscape orientation (wide).
fact: Orientation means the direction something faces or points.
fact: «Orientation» at school means a short welcome or tour that helps new pupils find their way.
fact: «Portrait orientation» means a page is tall; «landscape orientation» means it is wide.
fact: Orienteering is a sport where you use a map and a compass to find your way.
fact: Your sense of orientation tells you where you are and which way to go.
exercise: «The page was turned to landscape orientation.» What does orientation mean here? | A type of paper | A short school tour | A sport with a map | *The direction the page is facing or pointing
exercise: «On orientation day, the new pupils toured the school.» What is orientation day for? | To close the school for the summer | To paint the classroom walls | To test pupils on their maths | *To welcome new pupils and help them learn their way around
exercise: What tools do you use in orienteering to find your way? | A ruler and a pencil only | *A map and a compass | A football and a net | A recipe book and a spoon
test: «Tara's sense of orientation helped her find the school gate in the fog.» What does sense of orientation mean? | Losing your coat | Feeling cold in the fog | *Knowing where you are and which way to go | Liking to sing loudly
test: A rectangle is turned so it is tall, not wide. What is this called? | Orienteering | Landscape orientation | Orientation day | *Portrait orientation
exam: «Ben turned the map so north faced the top of the page, then used his compass to check his orientation.» What does orientation mean here? | His favourite food | A type of map paper | A short school welcome | *His direction and the way he is facing, found with a compass
